# Normalise line endings so the repository is byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout (where `core.autocrlf=true` is the git default)
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. That is not cosmetic here: the patch-hygiene
# suite splits source on '\n' and compares lines to their `trimEnd()`, so CRLF made
# it report hundreds of phantom trailing-whitespace offenders. The gate passed on
# Linux and failed on Windows.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to store LF in the object database and check out native
# endings; `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree too, which keeps the test's
# assumptions true everywhere. Binary assets are excluded explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images and other binaries must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Lockfiles are generated; normalising them creates noisy diffs.
package-lock.json -text
